{
  "name": "7-Segment LED Display Counter",
  "description": "A complete LED display subsystem: a 2-bit ripple counter (2 D flip-flops) drives gate logic that decodes the count to a real common-cathode 7-segment LED display (7 red LEDs with a realistic Vf≈1.9V model, 330Ω series resistors, ~9mA per segment). Run a transient (400µs, 200n step) and watch the segment currents: the display counts 1 → 2 → 3 → 0, one digit per 100µs clock period. Probe i(RA1)…i(RG1) for the segments. (Validated on ngspice: every digit phase shows the exact standard segment pattern.)",
  "tags": [
    "display",
    "led",
    "7-segment",
    "digital",
    "counter",
    "decoder",
    "mixed-signal"
  ],
